[09:32] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'directory, you can find them with a preset file name data set or you can change this to whatever you\'d like. All right, so my generation has finished and it should go without saying that it\'s going to take quite a while since you\'re generating 50 different images and'

[09:44] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'you\'re passing through two different models and then a face and eye detailer pass for each of those images. But it\'s worth it because you get a really quality data set out of it. You can see here that on my 5090, so 32 GB VRAM with 64 GB of system RAM, it took 13 minutes'

[09:58] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'and 7 seconds. So actually it\'s really not that bad. But we can see that we have a ton of images of different expressions, different angles, different POVs, getting the full scope of my character\'s body and identity and'

[10:11] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'features. So now what I\'m going to do is I\'m going to comb through the images and I\'m just going to delete any that I don\'t want. Maybe she has three arms in one picture or maybe the eyes are a different color in a different picture.'

[10:24] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'And I\'m just going to get rid of those images that I obviously don\'t want. And I highly suggest that you do the same thing. You don\'t want to just dump all of them straight into the training. Go through every single one and pull anything that came out wrong. So, if'

[10:36] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'there\'s extra fingers, a warped hand, a body that reads as distorted or dysmorphic, a face that drifted off identity, because when you\'re generating a data set with AI, it\'s not going to nail every single generation. And that\'s normal. But it\'s important that you come'

[10:48] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'through your data set generations because if you train on a data set with a handful of broken bodies or faces mixed in, the Laura will learn those broken proportions right along with everything else. I always say that a clean data set of 40 images beats a data'

[11:01] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'set of 50 images with five bad ones or 10 bad ones in it every single time. There\'s no magic number. 50 is not the magic number. 40 is not the magic number. It\'s just a matter of good quality input going into your training'

[11:14] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'means good quality output from the training. And the same goes for bad quality input. Bad quality input, bad quality output. I am going to be using Astress AI toolkit through RunPod today for the lower training process. Although'

[11:26] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'I have a 5090 and could do this training locally, I would rather put all the stress on my hardware that Laura training typically comes with onto a cloud services hardware instead. So that way my GPU stays nice and cool throughout the training process, which'

[11:38] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'can take upwards of 2 to 3 hours or more depending on the GPU that you use or have. And I can use my computer for other tasks while the Laura trains. Because if I were to train this locally, this would put a lot of stress on my'

[11:50] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'hardware and basically make my computer unusable during the entire training process. So, I\'m just going to use a throwaway pod for this by selecting a GPU with at least 32 GB of VRAM. I\'m going to be using the L40S for this'

[12:02] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
