VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'tokens and click that. From there, you\'ll see the create new token option. Click that. Once that interface is open, write any name in for the token name and select readon as well, both highlighted on screen. And once you\'ve done that,'

[14:09] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'create the token and then copy and paste that token into the settings tab on AI toolkit and click save to save the access token. Now we can go ahead with uploading our data set. So in the data set tab on the AI toolkit interface, I\'m going to click new data set in the top'

[14:23] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'right corner. And then I\'m going to write a name for the data set. So I\'m literally just going to write data set for this. And then I\'m simply going to drag and drop the folder that has all my data set images from my Comfy UI directory on my local device right into'

[14:35] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'there. and it\'s going to upload every single image. This should take only a few seconds. And now that the data set is fully uploaded, I am going to autocaption these images. So using the auto caption feature in the top right,'

[14:47] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'we can see a button for that. I\'m going to use the Quen 3 VL captioner built into AI toolkit. Now you can see here that there is a custom system prompt that we need to modify because obviously by default it is not going to do what we'

[14:59] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'want it to do. The system prompt I will be using can be found in the description of the video. This is basically going to instruct the Quen 3VL captioning model on how to caption our data set images and it\'s going to caption them in the'

[15:12] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'way that is preferred for character lura training. So now that I have that pasted in there, I\'m just going to add this to Q. We can see that the auto captioning process has begun and it\'s going to have to download the Quen 3VL model and then caption these images. So this may take a'

[15:26] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'few minutes. All right, so we can see that the captioning here has been completed. And if we take a look at the captioning, we can see that we have very short and concise captions. And the general rule of thumb for captions that you use on your images is this. The'

[15:38] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'things you described get marked as variable. So the model learns that they can change. So you want to describe things like the outfit, the setting, and so on. And the things that you do not describe get absorbed silently into the'

[15:50] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'trigger words identity. The model learns that they are fixed. And this is intentional and important. If you want the hair color locked into your character permanently, do not caption it. If you want the user to be able to change the hair color at generation time'

[16:03] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'when using the Laura in a workflow, then caption it. The face should never be captioned because it\'s part of the subject\'s identity and must be learned inside of the trigger token. So, do not caption things like eye color, skin'

[16:15] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'complexion, hair color, and so on if you do not want them to be changed. So, now that we have our data set uploaded and captioned, it\'s time to move on to the meat and potatoes, so to speak, of lura training that will actually get your'

[16:28] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'lura looking right. So, we\'re going to click new job on the lefth hand side of the ostrich AI toolkit. And the first thing that we are going to be changing here is the model that we are training the Laura on. So, I use Crea 2 Turbo when generating images with all my character lures. But even with that'

[16:41] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'being true, I am not going to train on Craya 2 Turbo. I am going to train on Craya 2 RAW. Training on Craya 2 Turbo is bad. Never do that. It does not provide good results at all. Something is wrong with it. I don\'t know what\'s'

[16:53] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'wrong with it, but I learned that the hard way. So, I am going to select create it to raw. And we can see here that it is a gated model, but we have already accepted the license for the gated model and uploaded our hugging'

[17:05] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'face token. So, you don\'t need to worry about that. Now, let\'s move on to some config settings. So, the first thing I\'m going to do is change the name of the file. So, something like Alyssa Prey 2. And then I\'m going to change or'

[17:17] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'make a trigger word. And the trigger word should be a completely unique string that will be used in captions or prompts to trigger the Laura. So since I have made her name Alyssa, I will make the trigger word something like this, which is basically Alyssa but with'

[17:30] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'numbers. And what this does is avoids the prompts generating any photos of someone who may be famous and named Alyssa because we don\'t want our prompts to get confused with anybody else named'

[17:42] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Alyssa. So, use a unique string that maybe has some numbers in it as the trigger word. I\'m going to leave low VRAM ticked on. Even though I\'m using a GPU that has 48 GB of VRAM, I believe I\'m just going to leave that on. It'

[17:55] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'doesn\'t really change anything at all. There\'s no point to turn it off. Moving on, I\'m going to keep save every at 250, but I\'m going to change the max steps to save to 10. So, this way, the maximum amount of checkpoints that we can save and are available for us to download is'

[18:08] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'at least 10. Leaving everything at the top the same, we\'re going to move down and I\'m going to check cache text embeddings. So, let\'s turn that on. And scrolling down from that, under data sets, I\'m going to make sure that our'

[18:20] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'data set is selected here. And I\'m basically going to leave everything else here the same. Make sure that you have at least 512, 768, and 1024 all selected as resolutions. This should be good enough. If you tick any of these higher'

[18:32] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'resolution settings, it\'s going to make the training process take exponentially longer. I don\'t think it\'s worth it at all. Some people even recommend turning both of these off and this will make the training process a lot faster, but it will train on lower quality images. So,'

[18:45] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'I\'m just going to leave these on. And moving down from data sets, we\'re going to take a look at the sampling section. Now, what this is is basically a way to generate samples throughout the training process at every x amount of steps. So,'

[18:57] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'by default, it\'s set at 250. So, every 250 steps, it\'s going to generate sample images to see how well the Laura has been trained. But this does not work with Craya. and it\'s a waste of time as well. I\'m going to show you a way to'

[19:10] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'check each one of your checkpoints using Comfy UI instead of using this built-in sampling because it does not do a great job and for Cray 2 in particular, it just doesn\'t work at all. I\'m going to completely disable sampling. We\'re going'

[19:22] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'to turn this off. And finally, I forgot to mention in data sets, I\'m also going to turn on cache latent. Make sure that you check that on. And aside from that, everything else can pretty much remain the same. Some people recommend using a'

[19:34] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'different training optimizer here. Atomw8 bit is selected by default and that\'s what I use. Some people say that automagic is good, but I\'ve tried it and the results did not come out as good as'

[19:46] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'the default Atomw8 bit. So, I\'m going to leave that and I\'m just going to create the job now. Now, once the job is created, you will see a play button in the top right corner and I am going to press the play button and this will'

[19:58] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'begin the training process and it will start downloading all of the models. And once the models are downloaded, it will begin the training process. So we can see here that it is loading the Cray 2 model and downloading them and they are quite large in size. So this is why this'

[20:11] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'is another benefit to using run pod and just using a throwaway pod is that you can download these models and it won\'t take up space on your local device. The best way to tell that the training process has begun is that you will see'

[20:24] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'here a progress bar at the very bottom of this terminal in the toolkit. and you\'ll see that the steps have begun iterating through the 3000step process of training the Laura. It can be argued that 3,000 steps is way more than what'

